<DocsLayout
  title="Rate Limit Stores - hitlimit | Memory, SQLite, Redis, Postgres, MongoDB, MySQL Storage Backends"
  description="Choose the right storage backend for your rate limiter. Compare memory, SQLite, Redis, Postgres, MongoDB, and MySQL stores for persistence, scalability, and performance. Easy migration between stores."
  keywords="rate limit store, redis rate limiter, sqlite rate limit, postgres rate limiter, mongodb rate limiter, mysql rate limiter, memory store, rate limit storage, distributed rate limiting, rate limit backend, persistent rate limit, bun rate limit store"
>
  <h1>Stores Overview</h1>

  <p>Stores are the backend that hitlimit uses to track request counts. Choose the right store based on your deployment needs.</p>

  <h2 id="available-stores">Available Stores</h2>

  <div data-runtime-content="node">
    <table class="stores-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Store</th><th>Persistence</th><th>Multi-instance</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/memory">Memory</a></td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Development, single instance</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/sqlite">SQLite</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td><td>Single server, persistence needed</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/redis">Redis</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed systems, high traffic</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/valkey">Valkey</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed, open-source Redis alternative</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/dragonfly">DragonflyDB</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>High-throughput distributed</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/postgres">Postgres</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed, existing Postgres infra</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/mongodb">MongoDB</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed, NoSQL / MEAN/MERN stacks</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/mysql">MySQL</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed, LAMP stacks / MariaDB</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div data-runtime-content="bun">
    <p>
      hitlimit-bun is <strong>memory-first by default</strong> with 12.3M+ ops/sec performance.
      Optional persistence available with native bun:sqlite (325K ops/sec), Redis (6.7K ops/sec), or Postgres (3.7K ops/sec) when you need it.
    </p>

    <table class="stores-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Store</th><th>Persistence</th><th>Multi-instance</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/memory">Memory</a></td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Default — 12.3M+ ops/sec</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/sqlite">SQLite</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td><td>bun:sqlite, zero deps — 325K ops/sec</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/redis">Redis</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed — 6.7K ops/sec</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/valkey">Valkey</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed, open-source — same as Redis</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/dragonfly">DragonflyDB</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>High-throughput distributed</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/postgres">Postgres</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed SQL — 3.7K ops/sec</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/mongodb">MongoDB</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed NoSQL</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/stores/mysql">MySQL</a></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Distributed SQL — MySQL/MariaDB</td></tr>
